\pard\sa20\par
\pard\s2\fs23\b\keepn\sb150\sa70 6 Cleaning and Interaction Weights\b0\par

\pard\s0\fs21\sa105\sl250\slmult1 Column names and event labels are normalised. Rows with missing required fields or unsupported event types are removed, followed by duplicate event removal. Events are ordered by time. The saved clean data contains 2,664,312 views, 69,332 cart additions and 22,457 transactions, showing that most feedback consists of browsing activity.\b0\par

\pard\s0\fs21\sa105\sl250\slmult1 Views receive weight 1, cart additions weight 3 and transactions weight 5. For each user-product pair, the weights of training events are summed and capped at 15. This makes stronger actions more influential while limiting repeated activity. These weights are modelling assumptions rather than probabilities or learned purchase preferences.\b0\par

\pard\s2\fs23\b\keepn\sb150\sa70 7 Temporal Split and Activity Filtering\b0\par

\pard\s0\fs21\sa105\sl250\slmult1 A global timestamp cutoff separates approximately the earliest 80% of events for training from the latest 20% for testing. The saved cutoff is 18 August 2015 at 04:23:20.445. Training uses timestamps strictly below the cutoff. This preserves the order in which interactions became available.\b0\par

\pard\s0\fs21\sa105\sl250\slmult1 After training events are aggregated, users with more than 500 distinct products are removed as potentially automated visitors. Products with fewer than five users and users with fewer than five products are removed iteratively. The resulting active population contains 16,053 users, 12,015 products and 152,818 pairs. Filtering depends only on training data.\b0\par

\pard\s2\fs23\b\keepn\sb150\sa70 8 Ground Truth\b0\par

\pard\s0\fs21\sa105\sl250\slmult1 A relevant test item must belong to the training catalogue and be new to that user. Test users must also exist in training. Of 308,551 test-period visitors, 1,425 remain known training users and 861 have eligible new products. Their average relevant set contains approximately 5.50 products. This restriction is essential when interpreting the evaluation coverage.\b0\par

\page
\pard\s1\fs32\b\keepn\sa160 System Architecture and Graph Model\b0\par

\pard\s2\fs23\b\keepn\sb150\sa70 9 Processing Architecture\b0\par

\pard\s0\fs21\sa105\sl250\slmult1 The project has two stages. The Phase 1 notebook prepares the raw data, fits the models, evaluates recommendations and exports artifacts. The Phase 2 Python application loads those artifacts and provides live recommendations through Streamlit. This avoids repeating full model construction whenever a user opens the dashboard.\b0\par

